<title>JAPAN: Sakura shares up on buy-back report.</title>
<headline>Sakura shares up on buy-back report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sakura Bank Ltd climbed on Tuesday morning, helped by a newspaper report saying that the commercial bank plans to buy back up to 350 million of its own shares, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0043 GMT, Sakura was up 10 yen at 852, after briefly rising to 870. Its volume was the heaviest on the first section at 3.178 million shares.  </p>
<p>Sakura Bank later confirmed the newspaper report.</p>
<p>A Sakura Bank spokesman said the share repurchase is aimed at improving the company's return-on-equity ratio.</p>
<p>The timing of the buy-back will be decided with consideration to the bank's business performance, he said.</p>
</text>
